---
import { agencyBenchmarks } from '../lib/agency-benchmarks';
import { asset } from '../lib/site';
---

<details class="comparison-methodology" id="comparison-methodology">
  <summary>How these agency estimates were modeled</summary>
  <div class="methodology-content">
    <p>
      The two endpoints use the same modeled human delivery hours and comparable-service scopes: the
      SMB base fee and the enterprise base fee from one hypothetical agency model, prepared October
      18, 2026. Each workstream's hours are multiplied by its client billing rate, then added and
      rounded to the nearest $100. The rates already include ordinary overhead and profit; no second
      markup is added.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>These are modeled estimates, not surveyed quotes or empirical market medians.</strong>
      SMB and enterprise describe two staffing and commercial rate cards, not a price determined solely
      by a client's company size. The endpoints are base scenarios, not the model's low/high bounds.
      The “+” means actual fees may be higher; it is not a measured upper limit. “Industry standard”
      describes the general cost-projection method, not independent certification of these prices or
      scopes.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong
        >The following quantities are comparison assumptions, not added FM contract terms.</strong
      >
      FM's 20 social posts per month are specified; article quantity and length, newsletter cadence and
      list-growth workload, and maintenance allowance and coverage still need agreement. In particular,
      two articles, two newsletter issues and four routine support hours are the selected comparison
      scenarios, not unlimited-delivery promises. Each FM service remains separately contracted at $400
      per month, month-to-month, or $400 one time, as shown.
    </p>
    <ol class="methodology-scopes">
      {
        agencyBenchmarks.map((benchmark) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{benchmark.title}</h3>
            <p class="methodology-fee">
              {benchmark.price} {benchmark.period}
            </p>
            <p>{benchmark.modelScope}</p>
            {benchmark.onboardingPrice && (
              <p class="methodology-onboarding">
                Separate modeled onboarding: {benchmark.onboardingPrice} one time (SMB base to
                enterprise base).
              </p>
            )}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
    <p>
      Recurring onboarding is separate from the monthly figures. The four one-time projects already
      include their own briefing and project management. Ad spend, software, hosting, domains, stock
      licenses, other third-party expenses and applicable taxes are excluded from the agency model.
      Additional FM costs are disclosed before agreement. This preview accepts no payment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each recurring figure includes account governance for a standalone service. Do not add the
      eleven comparisons into a bundle: that would count shared governance more than once. The
      animation illustrates FM's fee; it is not a calculated saving or a guarantee of equal
      deliverables. Full role hours, revision assumptions, exclusions, rate cards and calculations
      are retained in the supporting research.
    </p>
    <ul class="methodology-downloads">
      <li>
        <a href={asset('/research/agency-range-smb-enterprise-report-2026-10-18.md')}>
          SMB and enterprise model report (Markdown)
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={asset('/research/agency-range-smb-enterprise-model-2026-10-18.json')}>
          Both rate cards and calculations (JSON)
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={asset('/research/agency-range-human-hours-enterprise-report-2026-10-18.md')}>
          Original human-hours and enterprise research (Markdown)
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={asset('/research/agency-range-human-hours-enterprise-model-2026-10-18.json')}>
          Original two-phase model (JSON)
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={asset('/research/agency-range-selected-basis-2026-10-18.json')}>
          Selected endpoints and source register (JSON)
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</details>

<style>
  .comparison-methodology {
    margin-top: 20px;
    border: 1px solid #b9c8d6;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--ink);
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }
  summary {
    padding: 18px 22px;
    min-height: 44px;
    color: var(--blue);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #bf6200;
    outline-offset: 3px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .methodology-content {
    padding: 0 22px 22px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .methodology-content p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .methodology-scopes {
    padding-left: 22px;
    margin: 22px 0;
  }
  .methodology-scopes li {
    padding: 16px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #e0e8ef;
  }
  .methodology-scopes h3 {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0 0 5px;
  }
  .methodology-scopes p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .methodology-fee {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--blue);
  }
  .methodology-onboarding {
    color: #43576a;
  }
  .methodology-downloads {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .methodology-downloads a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 9px 0;
    min-height: 44px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  @media (max-width: 479px) {
    summary {
      padding: 16px;
    }
    .methodology-content {
      padding: 0 16px 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
